          "date": "2026-11-11 19:24:10.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-11509 ldlm: cancel privileged locks before replay",
        "message": "LU-11509 ldlm: cancel privileged locks before replay\n\nWith the LFRU lock cache an unused lock that was reused stays on\nns_unused_priv_list, which ldlm_prepare_lru_list() does not scan.\nThe cancel of unused locks before replay asks for ns_nr_unused\nlocks, so at most LDLM_LFRU_PRIV_PER_ROUND_LIMIT privileged locks\nare demoted to the normal list, and the rest are replayed.\n\nAsk for INT_MAX locks in ldlm_cancel_unused_locks_for_replay(), as\nlru_size=clear does, so that the whole privileged list is demoted\nand scanned.\n\nFixes: 0373d0c40b2f (\"LU-11509 ldlm: replace client lock LRU with LFRU\")\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Idf523c5b80cd0c13576fafa4ff928bf06a6a6964\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
